    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the soft-duplicate (\"possible duplicate\") rule for owner creation, keeping each piece of logic in its own small unit and reusing existing collaborators.\n\n**The rule**: after the existing hard-duplicate check passes, if a new owner shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` but has a *different* telephone, it's still created and flagged with `possibleDuplicate: true` / `possibleDuplicateOf: <matching owner id>`; otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`PossibleDuplicateDetector`** (new component, `rest.controller`) \u2014 single responsibility: finds the earliest existing owner sharing the candidate's last name + postcode with a different telephone, and records the outcome on the candidate. It reuses `ClinicService.findOwnerByLastNameIgnoreCase` (same lookup the household logic uses), mirroring the style of the sibling `IdentityDuplicateValidator` / `HouseholdAssigner`.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 wired the detector in as one line (`possibleDuplicateDetector.detect(owner)`) right after the hard-duplicate validation and before save, so the \"not a hard duplicate\" precondition is guaranteed.\n\n3. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added persisted `possibleDuplicate` (Boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (Integer) fields with columns, following the existing derived-field pattern (like `namesakeCount`), so the values computed at create time are read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the two read-only properties to the `Owner` schema, which generates the corresponding `OwnerDto` fields (auto-mapped by MapStruct).\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added `ignore` entries for the two read-only fields on the write-side `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` mapping, consistent with the existing ignores.\n\n6. **Schema SQL** (h2, hsqldb, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns so every DB profile matches the entity.",
